{
  "description": "A diagnosis adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the trained recommender through a stable compatibility interface and generates an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Support evidence-based model improvements while preserving RecHarness evaluation comparability and avoiding assumptions about unavailable reviews, item attributes, or simulator traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions. Probe view.model as the actual trained nn.Module; adapt feature and scoring probes when the architecture changes. Batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B x L. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Mark unavailable information as unobserved. Preserve all four datasets and routing, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, and DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five per category. Select trials using macro validation HR@10 under the pinned evaluator. Update the predictor writer whenever inference changes.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    initialize(view, device)\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        switch view.model to evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            collect supported measurements from histories and batches\n            obtain features and scores through architecture-compatible methods\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: measured_values, metric_definitions: definitions}\n\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    render measured metrics alongside their definitions\n    state missing evidence explicitly\n    request grounded interpretations and testable model changes",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic interface with explicit evidence and benchmark constraints.",
    "negative": "The supplied content specifies an adapter contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or diagnostic method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support comparable diagnosis across architecture changes and iterative recommendation experiments.",
    "negative": "Its value depends on the quality of implemented probes and whether their findings improve validation HR@10."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interface and batch format are explicit.",
    "negative": "Architecture-specific probing, faithful metric definitions, and synchronized predictor generation require careful implementation."
  }
}
